<title>USA: U.S. soybean weekly export sales highlights -U SDA.</title>
<headline>U.S. soybean weekly export sales highlights -U SDA.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-09-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. soybean major sales activity in the week ended Aug 29 reported by exporters for the following purchasing countries, in tonnes:</p>
<p>Net Sales:  1995/96		     1996/97</p>
<p>Netherlands  46,400		Taiwan    195,000</p>
<p>S. Korea     30,000		Unknown   161,000</p>
<p>Germany	 9,100</p>
<p>Unknown     -91,000-A</p>
<p>Norway	-33,000</p>
<p>A- changed to 1996/97.</p>
<p>Weekly exports of 200,800 tonnes were down 46 percent from the previous week and 38 percent below the four-week average.</p>
<p>Primary Export Destinations: Taiwan, Netherlands, Mexico and Japan.</p>
</text>
